Buy more at discount!
Nanjing Real Estate Market Reappears "Price Difference Compensation" - China News Service
Suzhou Evening News reports (by reporter Ma Zu-bo): On October 10th, while interviewing with reporters in Nanjing, we found that a 'guaranteed compensation clause' had once again returned to the real estate market of Nanjing after over ten years without appearing, and there is a property development company near Jiangbei New District that promises compensation for price differences, and during the time before handing over the house, other houses have greater discounts than the previous one-off discount; developers are willing to help buyers exchange their properties and return the difference.
There is no shortage of conditions under a "Guaranteed Value Agreement."
The property in this location at Jiangbei New District is known as Baoji Yangzi Cuiyun Tai; Mr. Sun, a prospective buyer who came to view the楼盘, told us that he noticed a "notification" while touring last weekend.
His pictures sent to the journalist show that the developer of this project promised that if buyers purchase their housing during the period from February 1st to February 28th, they can have the right to change and refund the difference in price after both parties sign the sale contract up until delivery of corresponding property. If other properties of the same floor type, unit, etc., within the building or community with an advantage over those sold at earlier times exist (up to the level where it's not the same floor type), the developer shall offer buyers exchange privilege for such properties and refund any additional prices incurred.
Mr. Sun said that the sales consultant explained that this was just an “insurance agreement” – to give buyers peace of mind when they sell and not worry about developers lowering their prices for promotional purposes. "Now I’m afraid that once we buy it, it will be lowered in price anyway; going to the sales office to protest won’t leave me time to do so, and if I don’t protest, it’s really nice."
There is still another group of homebuyers who think that while “guaranteed price agreements” are given to buyers as a promise to keep them calm, the terms are not so low.
Ms Zheng, who is planning to buy an affordable property in Jiangbei, says that properties with price guarantees must be of the same model and have similar layouts within the same building as well as in the same unit, so there aren’t many comparable options for buyers anyway. Thus, the threshold remains high.
There are also buyers who think that because of information asymmetry, salespeople may not exclude offering additional discounts, making it hard for them to protect their interests.
Whether it is possible to retain buyers remains to be seen.
The reporter learned through online real estate in Nanjing that the residential building sold off 252 units of two buildings last November with an average unit price per square meter of RMB 39,843 for fully furnished housing and ranging from 105 to 129 square meters in area.
But just over two months have passed since then, and online real estate currently displays that this project's total number of unsold units is 157 units (or 62.3%), with an additional 113 of those being unsold in building 8, while also having four units not sold out of building 7, for a total transactional sale of only 33 units or only about 13%.
Market observers note that the insurance protocol was also offered in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of last year, when Huaxiang West苑 on Heshan Mount Huangshan in Wuhu City promised to attract buyers with an 'Offer Guarantee Plan', it said that if any price discount were raised within a year, the company would return the difference back to the original owners as compensation for the lost revenue.
Starting in April 2011, nine residential properties in Nanjing also made commitments to refund “the difference” on some of their units.
"The real estate market is recovering; at this point, we need something to give it a kick in the pants."
Senior developer of the real estate industry in Nanjing said that "stabilized price" agreements also belong to marketing strategies employed by developers.
He believes that now enterprises need more confidence than home buyers, and offering the ‘guaranteed price’ policy is actually giving them encouragement.
In terms of whether one can retain home buyers, he said it depends on multiple factors such as control policies and loan thresholds, among others, which will have to be observed for now.
China's rescue team continues to carry out rescue operations in Turkey and has rescued four trapped individuals so far - Xinhua News Agency
China News Service (CNS) reported on February 11 that, according to information from the website of the Ministry of Emergency Management, two rescuers and one survivor were retrieved in an emergency operation conducted by China’s rescue team that was searching for people trapped under debris in Turkey.
Two search and assessment teams were dispatched to assess and investigate 15 buildings on Wadaibashi Street at the same time.
So far, four people trapped have been rescued and five others killed have been located; assessments of life signs and risks at 25 collapsed structures have been carried out.
The rescue team will adjust its relief force scientifically based on the actual situation in the disaster area and conditions at the scene of assistance. It will continue to deepen the rescue work.
The rescue team obtained information on assistance requests through multiple channels such as embassies, local governments, and UN relief organizations, verified them through various means including online inquiries and on-site searches.
To introduce the current rescue environment and conditions of building collapses to China’s Hong Kong Rescue Team and jointly carry out search operations.
Currently coordinating with the Italian search and rescue team for regional coordination (SSC5), while sending three members to work at the 5th Regional Search and Rescue Coordination Center in charge of operations, they communicated with multiple teams from Italy, Britain, Serbia, Slovakia, Oman, etc., learned about the UN rescue organization's operation and the situation of rescue teams from various countries.
The rescue teams continue to strengthen safety management and personnel support operations in accordance with the principle of unified command and prioritizing safety; they reinforce on-site safety control, enhance the enforcement requirements for rescue work, and clarify safety precautions.
Continued execution of rotating watch and sentry duty systems for ongoing operation, enhancing camp area security management.
The medical staff of rescue teams provide physical examinations for team members on an ongoing basis and enhance health protection measures for key personnel. At present, all members of the rescue team are physically fit and healthy; they have carried out disinfection operations in their base camp.
After establishing their own campsite, the logistics support team has set up 4 major categories of tents – command communication, equipment storage, medical decontamination, living accommodation, and dog kennels – totaling 26 tents to ensure that more than 30 sets of on-site rescue equipment were available for use.
Kim Jong-nam and his daughter have close father-daughter interactions, but his wife is left out in the cold.
(Reuters) North Korea held a military parade on Saturday evening to mark the 75th anniversary of建军節, with Pres. Kim Jong Un’s daughter Kim Ryong-eun attending and joining her father at the podium.
Korea’s state media aired videos showing Kim Il-sung holding his daughter and tenderly looking at her several times while whispering to her, as he gently brushed his daughter’s cheeks with his hands, or even touched her father's chest. The footage of the father-daughter interaction was broadcast nationwide.
However, First Lady Li Xuehua is relegated to the sidelines.
According to reports from “Korean Central News Agency” and others, Kim Jong-nam and Ri Sol-ju were seen at an official photo of their daughter Kim Jung-a attending a banquet on July 7th. Kim Jung-a was not only rarely sitting in the middle C position with her parents but also joined Kim Jong-nam together with him on the podium for the military parade celebrating the 75th anniversary of建军节.
The "Korean Central Television" of North Korea released footage after the military parade showing more scenes of father and daughter love.
Kim Jong-nam frequently looked at his daughter with one glance from behind the podium, their faces never lost smiling and whispering to each other in each others’ ears; Kim Jong-il once hugged his father’s cheeks with both hands while Kim Jong-un responded with laughter.
Other official media frames show that when Kim Yo Jong sat with Kim Jong Nam in an indoor sofa chair, she constantly stroked her father’s face; and while walking alongside her father, who was holding her hand, she touched Kim Jong Nam on his chest.
And First Lady Li Xiaomei had to walk behind or sit aside all the time, always remaining several steps away from her husband and daughter.
The media in South Korea has pointed out that Kim Jong Un’s presence has increased three months after his first public appearance on October 18 last year. Since then he has appeared five times at formal occasions.
The North Korean media has referred to Kim Jong-nam as "the dearest sons and daughters" or "honorable sons and daughters." It also aired footage of Kim Jong-nam watching the military parade from the stands, shouting incoherently over and over “I shall always uphold bloodline” throughout.
These signals have led outside observers to doubt whether Kim Il-sung’s successor is already chosen, and The Washington Post analysts saw in that as a signal for Kim Jong-un putting his teenage daughter on the throne. However, some believe that this assessment may still be premature since there are various possibilities still available when it comes to the succession of Kim Jong-un who has a son at his side.
"ETF Account Here: CSRC Authorizes Development of Investment Fund Aggregation and Inquiry for Investors' Portfolios" – Economic Observer (Professional Financial News Website)
Economic Observer reporter Chen Shan The difficulty of aggregating account information due to the complexity of fund purchase channels?
Always forgetting about "the little gold pig"?
The issues of the Kiehm will soon be resolved.
On February 10th, the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) announced that “Fund E Account” APP had been uploaded to and in public trial operation on all mobile application stores.
According to the introduction, "Fund E Account" provides one-stop service for individual investors to query information on all kinds of open-end funds including account number and share details, aiming at solving industry pain points such as forgotten account numbers and cumbersome inquiry processes among large number of small and medium-sized investors.
According to Wind data, at the end of 2022, there were approximately 156 domestic fund management companies, and the managed assets reached about RMB 2.6 trillion; there were approximately 167 fund share registration institutions for funds, as well as 411 fund sales institutions.
Each share registration institution's account system is independent and lacks an industry-wide query channel.
Industry observers say that at the end of 2021, there were over 72 million fund investors in China, meaning that half of the country’s population had invested in funds.
Previously, investors had to query their purchase status through different sales institutions; now they can view all of their purchases on the “Fund E Account,” which makes it easy to see their holdings.
What is the "Fund E Account" APP?
According to relevant documents, “Fund E Account” App is a mobile application that was developed and approved by China Securities Depository and Clearing Co., Ltd. under the auspices of the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC), serving as an all-inclusive platform for investors to obtain real-time holdings information on open-market shares held in the full market range of open-end funds.
Investors can conveniently and efficiently know their holdings of all fund products offered through various sales channels by using the “Fund E Account”. This will enhance the efficiency of queries significantly.
Specifically, investors can obtain information through “Fund E Account”, such as fund account information for all open-end fund management companies in the market, transaction account information at public mutual funds sales institutions, and the number of individual holders for products including publicly offered securities investment funds without restrictions on 200 people and collective asset management plans set up and managed by securities companies.
Bloomberg's head of fund evaluation at Shanghai Securities Fund Evaluation Research Center, Liu Yikang, told Caixin that investors can obtain all their onshore open-end fund holdings through the "Fund E Account" App in one go and help them recover 'forgotten assets'. More importantly, it has enabled customers to aggregate comprehensive information about their investment situation across accounts, helping them better understand their own investment status more promptly, accurately, and comprehensively, thereby optimizing their fund portfolio configuration and planning their financial arrangements accordingly.
How do you register and use it?
Journalists noted that “Fund E Account” App was available on Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, Vivo and other smartphone application stores but is currently undergoing public trial run; registration requires an invitation code to be filled in, and investors can contact the fund management companies holding their respective funds for assistance.
A fund manager of Shanghai's large-scale public equity fund provided an invitation code to an economic observer reporter and said that during the trial operation phase of the APP, China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation gave each fund manager a certain number of invitation codes. Investors called for these codes, and we would all provide them.
Once the trial period is over, there will be no need for invitation codes to register users.
Translation requested.
Journalists registered and used their accounts as instructed on Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) website's "Fund E Account" download and use guide within minutes. The whole process was mainly divided into four steps: user registration, identity verification, fund account binding, and inquiry of open-end funds.
After completing this step of real-name authentication, clicking on the “Asset Fund Binding” button allows journalists to see all their purchased fund products from various fund sales platforms listed in the binding options (which can be linked to an account). After successful binding, they will be able to intuitively view their total investment in funds and start using the query function.
It is worth noting that “Fund E Account” provides query services for investors and does not allow redemption or subscription transactions.
The data shown for Fund E account is typically three trading days prior to the date the user queries (T day).
For example, on February 10th, when you open the "Fund E Account," the total assets, fund shares, and net asset value displayed under the Asset page correspond to the date three trading days prior to that, which is February 7th.
