Multi-sectoral decline in economic data shows poor start of year for Taiwan's economy - Xinhua
Xinhua Taiwan, Feb 11 (Reporter Zhao Bo and Huang Yang): Total exports for this year have been running five red lines in a row; the Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) of manufacturing has been contracting for seven consecutive months; Consumer Price Indexes have also hit their ‘thrice-digit’ territory once again... In recent days, Taiwan’s government has successively released economic data from January.
Experts say that Taiwan's economy is underperforming in the new year, and growth pressures are mounting.
According to Taiwan’s financial and taxation bureau, Taiwan region exports in January this year reached $3. 151 billion US, a decrease of 21.2% from last year and it was a negative growth for the fifth consecutive month.
The export value of 11 major product categories declined compared with that of last year.
Plastic rubber and its products, as well as optical instruments, had the sharpest declines of 37.6% and 35.7%, respectively.
Electronic components exports fell 20.1% year on year, marking the largest decline in over a decade.
Among them, integrated circuits fell 18.3%, marking their largest decline in nearly a decade.
Cai Meina of the Bureau of Statistics said that this shows the impact from the sluggish demand in consumer electronics to expand and that the electronics industry is entering an adjustment period.
Statistics show that Taiwan’s exports and imports fell in January for the second consecutive month, with the deficit amounting to only $2. 34 billion, its lowest level since 2007.
The Taiwan authorities’ finance bureau believes that global terminal demand is declining, industrial adjustments in inventory will suppress manufacturers' purchasing intentions for materials, and export weakness may not improve temporarily. The Taiwanese first-quarter exports could be worse than expected this year.
The Central Economic Research Institute of Taiwan's China Economy Association reported that in January this year, the purchasing managers' index for manufacturing in Taiwan was adjusted seasonally and stood at 40.4%, down by 3.3 percentage points from its level last December, indicating a decline over the preceding seven months.
In the economic monitoring index system, PMI is at 50% as the turning point for health and illness; an index greater than 50% indicates expansion of prosperity, while less than 50% signifies contraction.
In January, five of the PMI's six indicators in Taiwan, namely new orders, production, and manpower employment fell, while supplier delivery times shortened and inventory tightened.
All six industries registered PMI contractions and ranked according to their contraction rates as follows: Electrical and machinery industry (35.1%), Electronic and optical industry (35.2%), Chemicals and biotechnology medical equipment industry (39.2%), Raw materials sector (42.4%), Transportation equipment industry (42.6%), and Textile and food processing industries (45.7%).
On prices, figures released by the Mainland Affairs Council’s National Statistics Office indicate a year-on-year increase of 3.04% in consumer price index (CPI) for Taiwan in January this year, breaking the 3%-level again since July last year.
Among them, vegetable prices jumped 28.25%, reaching their highest level in 17 months.
Committee Chairperson Mr. Cao Zhihong from the “Director General’s Office of Statistics,” acknowledged that price increases had exceeded expectations. Even if we exclude factors such as the Spring Festival and other seasonal influences, the year-on-year inflation rate for January and February this year should be close to the 2.71% in December last year. Inflationary pressure is still present, albeit at high levels.
Looking ahead to Taiwan’s economy this year, experts are pessimistic according to reporting from media outlets such as “United Daily News” and Yahoo Finance on the island.
Professor Wu Daren from the “Central University of Taiwan’s School of Economics” has warned that exports slowing down could result in cash flow problems for export manufacturing firms and higher risks of defaulting on debt.
At the same time, falling orders have caused producers to reduce labor costs and impact the labor market and household economies, which in turn hit consumption capacity.
Mr. Chou Ta-sing of the Institute of Taiwan Economic Research believes that the inflation situation in Europe and America is not resolved this year, and demand continues to shrink. Consequently, he forecasts that Taiwanese export will continue to suffer from decline throughout the first half of the year.
Since Taiwan’s economy relies on exports for support, and export demand is weakening, its overall growth performance over the year will likely be weaker than last year.
Central Committee members newly admitted to the Central Committee, alternate members of the Central Committee, and principal cadres at the provincial and ministerial level concluded the seminar on learning and implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress - Continuous News - Hupeng News - Huasheng Online
The newly elected members of the Politburo Standing Committee and alternate members of the Central Committee as well as leading cadres at provincial and ministerial levels have completed their training on learning and implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
2023-02-11 13:07:20 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Size: 【Large Medium Small】
Xinhua Beijing on February 10th: The training class for newly-inducted central committee members, alternate members and provincial and ministerial leading cadres on studying the thought of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era under Xi Jinping’s leadership concluded in the School of Party Affairs Research of the Central Party School (National Academy of Governance) after its afternoon session. At this graduation ceremony held jointly organized by the Secretariat of the CPC Central Committee and the Secretariat of the Communist Party of China Central Committee, Secretary of the Political Bureau of the Central Committee, Cai Qi, delivered a summary speech.
He said that he would thoroughly study and implement the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar training class, with greater determination to uphold the “two establishments” and resolutely achieve the “two upholds,” strengthen his abilities and work hard to advance all tasks related to China’s modernization in accordance with the requirements of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era, and create achievements worthy of historical, practical, and people's judgment in fully building a modern socialist country and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar period, all trainees studied the thought of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era under Xi Jinping, and learned about the important speeches delivered at the opening ceremony of the seminar by General Secretary Xi Jinping on behalf of the Central Committee of the CPC. They linked practice to in-depth study and discussion on major theoretical and practical issues concerning China’s modernization, thereby deepening their understanding of some key theories and practices related to the path of national rejuvenation through Chinese-style modernization. This strengthened their confidence and determination in leading the rejuvenation of the Chinese nation under the leadership of the Central Committee of the CPC led by Xi Jinping, as well as their sense of responsibility and mission towards fulfilling responsibilities and performing duties effectively and achieving a good start during the New Era and the new journey.
At the graduation ceremony, representatives from 10 of the seminar participants gave speeches and reports on their learning experiences.
Chai Qi noted that deepening study and implementation of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China is not just the first political task to be undertaken in the present period and beyond, but also an important long-term strategic undertaking, and it should adhere to the requirements of "comprehensive learning", "holistic grasp", and "complete execution" and push forward the learning and implementation work towards being more profound, concrete, and heartfelt.
To more deeply understand the decisive significance of “the two establishments,” we must resolutely uphold the core position of Xi Jinping and the authority of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi at its heart, as well as the centralized and unified leadership of the Party. We should continuously enhance our political judgment, political insight, and political execution, ensuring that we always maintain high consistency in thought, politics, and action with the Central Committee led by Comrade Xi.
It is important to master and grasp thoroughly Marxist theory as one’s forte, consciously using the party's innovative theories to arm one’s mind, guide practice, and drive work. One should strive in deep study, careful understanding, and earnestly implementing these efforts, so that they can truly cultivate strong political beliefs, absolute loyalty, and firm mission responsibilities.
To earnestly implement all decisions and deployments of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with an enterprising spirit, advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves to work hard, get down to business as a good “construction supervisor”, step by step turn the blueprint into reality.
To remember that reforming and governing the Party in an all-round way is an ongoing process and that self-revolution of the Party must also be ongoing, and to press hard for the political responsibility of comprehensive strict governance of the Party, with political building of the Party as its overarching priority, and advance the new great project of Party building in this new era.
To enhance capabilities to promote high-quality development, serve the people, and address risks, we should foster an atmosphere of mass investigations and research efforts, and resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucracy.
Zhai Tiefeng, Li Ganjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jinguo, and Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony. Chen Xi presided over it.
Xinhua Ha Noi – Xinhua reported that Vietnam’s Prime Minister Nguyen Xuanthu and his family successfully undertook official visits to Singapore and Brunei. The trip achieved comprehensive, pragmatic, and specific results.
Former Prime Minister FENG Mingzhi participated in 30 different events within three days of his visits to Singapore and Brunei.
The achievement injected new impetus for deepening, broader, and more effective strategic partnership between Vietnam and the newly established two Vietnameses.
During his visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chai reiterated Vietnam’s Party and state’s foreign policy of independence, diversity, adaptability and readiness to be a friend and reliable partner for all states, as well as a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in their respective countries' interests to improve people's wellbeing there and for peace, stability, and development in the region and around the world.
During each meeting and negotiation, Mr. Fan Mingzheng agreed with their respective leaders from Singapore and Brunei to strengthen political trust in Vietnam through inter-governmental visits of high-level delegations as well as effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and key partnership agreements.
Several cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam and Singapore have signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership.
Image from Vietnam News Agency
Pham Minh Chinh emphasized during meetings with business leaders, discussions, and participation in economic forums that Vietnam is open and supportive towards Singapore and Brunei investments in its digital transformation, green energy, high-tech fields as well as creative innovation activities, creating conducive conditions to expand their investment scope in these areas.
The visit will deepen cooperation among Vietnam, Singapore and Brunei in various traditional areas including politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education & training, oil and gas exploration, tourism and people-to-people exchanges. It will also create new potential areas of cooperation such as digital economy, green economy, energy transformation, innovation creativity, smart cities and sustainable development.
King Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah of Brunei and Premier Wen Jiabao are preparing to enter a bilateral meeting.
Image sourced from VNA News Agency
During his visits to both countries, Pham Minh Chinh’s Prime Minister has made time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of Vietnamese expatriates living there.
In bilateral meetings with President Hu and Mr. Fan Mingzheng, Prime Minister Chen stressed that both authorities should pay more attention to the local Vietnamese community’s fair treatment in society so as to create favorable conditions for the group to contribute to their societies and foster relations between China and Vietnam.
The proposals have been endorsed and supported by both leaders.
In particular, Vice President Fang Mingzheng also shared with the leaders of both countries his desire for an ASEAN Community that is united, peaceful, stable and prosperous; they agreed to maintain unity and cooperation with ASEAN member states while enhancing their role as a regional and international leader in the complex and ever-changing geopolitical environment.
With its important achievements, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh made an official visit to Singapore and Brunei to effectively implement the Party’s Third Congress’ priority of strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbors through effective implementation of the 12th Conclusion (12-KL/TW) of the Central Committee Political Bureau on Vietnamese Foreign Affairs in the new situation, as well as making positive contributions to mobilizing the strength of the entire nation.
(TERMINATION)
What was the "object" that was shot down over Al Ain?
Confusing and speculative
The US military on Friday afternoon (February 10) fired its most advanced stealth jet, the F-22, to down an unidentified object in flight over Alaska.
The location from which it was shot is ten miles south of Alaska's coast.
This is the second time in less than a week that US aircraft have downed an aerial object.
An air balloon operated from China that was spying on American communications in US airspace drifted for several days before it was shot down off the South Carolina coastline of the United States last Saturday.
The Pentagon said that the second object downed was first detected in US airspace on Thursday night as it moved northeast of Alaska and tracked by US military officials, flying at an altitude of 12,000 meters (approximately 40,000 feet), about the size of a small car – significantly smaller than the earlier downing of the China-based spy balloon.
The Pentagon still believes that there is no indication that it can be manipulated.
White House National Security Council Deputy Coordinator John Kobie Friday said that although the specific shape of this object flying at high altitude remained unclear, it posed a reasonable threat to the safety of commercial aircraft.
Kobe said that this object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which does not have an attached payload.
Kobe said that we called it an “object” because this is our best current description of what it is.
President Biden listened to Pentagon advice before ordering the destruction of the object and added that he made his decision “very carefully.”
The US official description of the object can be roughly summarized as follows: it is about the size of a small car; there is no steering wheel or suspension system; its flight height is around 10,000 meters.
But such information does not answer basic questions like what is this object, where it belongs and what mission it is executing.
Currently, many online analyses and speculations suggest this could be another Chinese hot air balloon.
They may all have come from China, like the spy balloon that flew over US airspace and the Chinese balloon floating above South America, performing some kind of mission at different locations.
There are those who link this Alaska "object" to UFOs (unidentified flying objects).
The report from Newsweek magazine cites former US Congressman Peter Meijer, who tweeted on Friday, “I really hope this ‘unidentified flying object’ is an espionage balloon rather than a legitimate UFO.”
The irony of conflating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is striking, but it does not warrant an interstellar conflict, he said.
Majedi tweeted just after Kobe confirmed that the object that was downed in Alaska had been shot down.
Newsweek says that it is not just Marchant who suspects this object to be an UFO.
Rep. Tim Burchett, Republican from Tennessee, has criticized the government’s cover-up of intelligence this month and demanded that the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) release reports on unidentified flying objects.
Iran marks anniversary of Islamic Revolution; hackers support protests against presidential televised address
Iran's Islamic Republic held an official rally on Saturday to mark the 44th anniversary of the Iranian revolution but interrupted President Ebrahim Raisi's televised address by brief hacking attacks.
The television address made by President’s live-streaming speech was interrupted for about a minute and then appeared a group of anti-Iranian government hackers with the name Edalat Ali (Ali Justice).
There was also a voice that shouted, “Islamic Republic dead.”
Reuters reported today that Iran is commemorating its revolution’s anniversary and cybercriminals have disrupted coverage of national television news.
Iranian officials mark 44th anniversary of Islamic Revolution; Shiraz’s hardliners face biggest challenge yet from young protesters demanding their ouster but still urges “deceived youth” to repent so they can be pardoned by Iran’s supreme leader.
Following the death of Mahsa Amini, aged just 22 and under Iran’s morality police custody in September, mass protests have erupted across the country.
The Iranian security forces have ruthlessly suppressed protests, making this one of the most powerful challenges to Islamic Republic since the overthrow of the monarchy in 1979.
As part of a gesture to mark the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities freed Friday two imprisoned dissidents whose arrest stemmed from hunger strikes: Faheem Mesami, who is also an Iranian-French scholar; and Fariba Adelkhah.
Earlier Ayatollah Ali Khameini issued an amnesty decree that included some prisoners arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to a Human Rights Activists Network report, at least 528 protesters had been killed as of Friday evening – including 71 minors.
The report says that another 70 government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and official media have been calling for an election to be held on Saturday in order to show their opposition to protest activity and support for the government.
On Friday evening of the 40th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, official media showed fireworks as part of a government-sponsored celebration, with people shouting “Allahu Akbar!”
(God is the greatest!)
However, there is also much shouting at the rallies in favor of “Death to Dictators!”
And death of the Islamic Republic in videos posted on social media.
Saturday, viewers across the country saw live footage of official meetings in their respective states broadcast on government television stations.
In Tehran as part of an official celebration, displays were held of domestically produced anti-ballistic missiles, drones, counter-submarine frigates, and other military equipment.
Lieber President Lewski’s speeches are frequently interrupted with the “get lost” chants – the hallmark of state gatherings.
The crowd shouted "Israel must die."
Reuters reported that Adelkhah, who has been in prison since at least 2019, was detained in Iran along with six other French nationals held there for months – one of several factors contributing to deteriorating relations between Paris and Tehran over recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 on charges of national security violations.
They later confined her to her house but she returned to prison in January.
Adelkhah denies these allegations.
And just one week before Mesa-Mi’s release, supporters warned that he faced a death risk due to his hunger strike.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting against mandatory headscarf wearing.
The French Ministry of Foreign Affairs responded on Friday to Adel Khah’s release and called for her freedom “including if she is willing, allowing her to return to France.”
