Full-time dedication to character and emotional arcs captivates readers deeply, with characters who barely appear having significant impressions; notable roles such as Xie Ye, Huang Shoutian, and Su Mo’er have numerous fans. Characters that don’t make the writing center are equally popular, such as Jiang Bopao and Chu Yunxiu, who are very easy to like in an e-sports novel where there is no extreme dislikeable person. This fully demonstrates the success of full-time in character depiction.
But on the emotional front, full-time doesn’t suffer from the kind of problem that most web novels have had with their palace beauties and three hundred million evil girls, where everyone’s love for them is either beautiful or degenerate. In the entire story, all people like this game, and they mostly want to win in an upright manner.
The little conspiracies have nothing big about them, and each of us seems so innocent and lovable.
This may well be why the full-time job does not have any unpleasant roles.
